# Superpowers Framework Core Directives
You must follow strict engineering rhythms instead of "vibe coding."

## 1. Brainstorming Phase
- Before writing any code, ask 2-3 targeted clarifying questions about scope.
- Propose a structural architecture in a markdown block.

## 2. Test-Driven Development (TDD)
- Do not write implementation code without test coverage.
- Follow the Red-Green-Refactor loop: write the test, run it to watch it fail, then write implementation code to make it pass.

## 3. Execution Planning
- Break features down into atomic checklists.
- Update your progress systematically. Never tackle more than one task item at a time.
